What is ELK Stack?
ELK = Elasticsearch + Logstash + Kibana
It's the world's most popular log management and analytics platform. 
Originally built by Elastic, it solves the "needle in a haystack" problem of finding errors across thousands of servers.


Why ELK over traditional logging?
# Traditional (grep on 100 servers):
ssh server01 "grep 'ERROR' /var/log/app.log"  # Takes hours

# ELK way:
# One Kibana query across ALL servers in < 1 second

2. Core Components & Their Functions
Elasticsearch (The Storage & Search Engine)
Role: Distributed RESTful search and analytics engine.

Key Concepts:

Concept	    Analogy	        ELK Reality
Index	    Database	    Container for similar logs (e.g., nginx-logs-2024.01.01)
Shard	    Partition	    An index broken into pieces for horizontal scaling
Replica	    Backup copy	    Prevents data loss if a node dies
Document	Row/Record	    A single log entry (JSON format)
Node	    Server	        One Elasticsearch instance


Real Example:

json
// What Elasticsearch stores (one document)
{
  "_index": "leopay-prod-2026.05.04",
  "_source": {
    "@timestamp": "2026-05-04T10:30:15Z",
    "service": "payment-gateway",
