  }
}



FLOW:
Complete Data Flow

[Application Server]                    [Central ELK Cluster]
---------------------                    --------------------

1. App writes log → /var/log/app.log
                    ↓
2. Filebeat detects change (inotify)
   - Reads new lines
   - Updates registry with offset
                    ↓ (TCP 5044)
3. Logstash receives via beats input
   - Goes to persistent queue (disk)
   - Pipeline processes batch
     • Grok parsing
     • Mutate fields  
     • GeoIP enrichment
                   ↓ (HTTP 9200)
4. Elasticsearch indexes
   - Routes to correct shard (hash based on _id)
   - Creates inverted index
   - Replicates to replica shards
                   ↓ (HTTP 5601)
5. Kibana queries via browser
   - User searches "ERROR"
   - Translates to ES REST API
   - Renders results

Actual Network Flow Example:

# On log generation (server side):
echo "2026-05-04 10:30:15 ERROR Payment failed" >> /var/log/payment.log

# What happens:
1. Kernel inotify tells Filebeat: file changed
2. Filebeat reads line → JSON wrapper:
   {"@timestamp":"2026-05-04T10:30:15Z","message":"Payment failed","service":"payment"}
3. TCP packet to Logstash:5044
4. Logstash acknowledges (ACK) - Filebeat can now remove from queue
5. Logstash transforms (grok, date, mutate)
6. HTTP POST to Elasticsearch:9200/_bulk
7. ES returns 201 Created
8. Kibana user sees it in < 1 second
